21-e216-553a-b3ca-72efe4f524e3" :answer-field/key "V" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440290}] :question/id #uuid "142e660e-5b1f-5e61-a343-ee1945f69615" :question/math-academy-id "q-65208" :question/problem "At which points on the curve $9x^{2}y = 3y^{3} - 6x$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $i$?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $(-1,-1)$\n- **II.** $(-1,1)$\n- **III.** $(0,0)$\n- **IV.** $(1,-1)$\n- **V.** $(1,1)$" :question/worked-solution "Write the curve as F(x,y)=0. A tangent is (F_y,-F_x); its dot product with the given vector is $9 x^{2} - 9 y^{2}$. Solving this with the curve equation gives $(-1,1), (0,0), (1,-1)$, and the tangent is nonzero at each point."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265855 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84245283-3cf9-5889-8c42-896a0c8af291" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points on a Curve at which the Tangent Vector is Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4be39072-497d-5f31-85ed-080e23888640" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263654} {:answer/id #uuid "c1a31d3c-8503-58a7-8ecf-53ce88e8429e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264681} {:answer/id #uuid "c5f465b6-bac3-55a1-8d75-c1289cf7313e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264733} {:answer/id #uuid "d297311d-d396-508d-a6bd-3e8b3fd8c863" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264836} {:answer/id #uuid "e32b090c-8a44-582a-8e53-682c5da583b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-12)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264972}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1a31d3c-8503-58a7-8ecf-53ce88e8429e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264681} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2ab0ddd-26ef-5f3a-b559-a55d7b1fb92f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265530}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1ac4e615-d461-5edb-9d78-97997efce275" :question/math-academy-id "q-130223" :question/problem "At which point on the curve ${x}^{2}y=-8x-4$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $j?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}y & =-8x-4 \\\\ {x}^{2}y+8x & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)={x}^{2}y+8x,$ our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=-4.$ \n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$\nt(x,y)={f}_{y}(x,y)\\,i-{f}_{x}(x,y)\\,j\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y) & ={f}_{y}(x,y)\\,i-{f}_{x}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y+8x)\\,i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y+8x)\\,j \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\,i-(2xy+8)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince our tangent vector needs to be perpendicular to $j,$ we must have $t\\cdot j=0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot j & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}\\,i-(2xy+8)\\,j)\\cdot j & =0 \\\\ -(2xy+8) & =0 \\\\ xy+4 & =0 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{4}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $y=-\\frac{4}{x}$ into the equation of our curve gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}y & =-8x-4 \\\\ {x}^{2}(-\\frac{4}{x}) & =-8x-4 \\\\ -4x & =-8x-4 \\\\ 4x & =-4 \\\\ x & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, for $x=-1,$ we get $y=4,$ and the corresponding point is $(-1,4).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339110 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84245283-3cf9-5889-8c42-896a0c8af291" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points on a Curve at which the Tangent Vector is Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c87