er/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521849} :answer-field/id #uuid "c455ae41-516c-5087-9292-187bc01c3ff1" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521850} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fe93697-ea3f-5119-a24f-b497681320d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521819} {:answer/id #uuid "9655312b-299c-5150-92fb-924ba2114fd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fe93697-ea3f-5119-a24f-b497681320d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521819} :answer-field/id #uuid "e41e89b0-8613-5944-9948-dba717ba611f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521860}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "10aa9a22-24d9-5578-9f7c-cc0b57f6bc72" :question/problem "At which points on the curve $8 x y + 2 y^{2}=16 x^{2} + 432$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $j$?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $(-3,-12)$\n- **II.** $(0,12)$\n- **III.** $(\\frac{3}{2},12)$\n- **IV.** $(3,0)$\n- **V.** $(3,6)$\n- **VI.** $(3,12)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}8 x y + 2 y^{2}&=16 x^{2} + 432\\\\- 16 x^{2} + 8 x y + 2 y^{2} - 432&=0\\end{aligned}$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)=- 16 x^{2} + 8 x y + 2 y^{2} - 432$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$\n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$t(x,y)=f_y(x,y)\\,i-f_x(x,y)\\,j$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)&=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- 16 x^{2} + 8 x y + 2 y^{2} - 432)\\,i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- 16 x^{2} + 8 x y + 2 y^{2} - 432)\\,j\\\\&=(8 x + 4 y)\\,i-(- 32 x + 8 y)\\,j\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSince our tangent vector needs to be perpendicular to $j$, we must have $t\\cdot j=0.$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot j&=0\\\\32 x - 8 y&=0\\\\y&=4x\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSubstituting $y=4x$ into the equation of our curve gives:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}2(4x)^{2}+8x(4x)-16x^{2}-432&=0\\\\48x^{2}-432&=0\\\\x^{2}&=9\\\\x&=\\pm 3\\end{aligned}$$\n\nFinally, the corresponding points are $(3,12)$ and $(-3,-12)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521761 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84245283-3cf9-5889-8c42-896a0c8af291" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points on a Curve at which the Tangent Vector is Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a67e1549-d894-58c3-ab0c-c5878c485999" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521835} {:answer/id #uuid "ee1f00c6-1b40-51e8-8084-53cf529cfa21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521867}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee1f00c6-1b40-51e8-8084-53cf529cfa21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521867} :answer-field/id #uuid "15959162-8202-56a1-a0f2-83319529d308" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521763} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1582ef11-2a8f-56b8-be1e-533ad686623d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521762} {:answer/id #uuid "4d90e1ca-3cff-5a39-9cbc-7a04878d8001" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d90e1ca-3cff-5a39-9cbc-7a04878d8001" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521796} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bf2940c-8256-52c6-be97-fc5e2aae3edc" :answer-field/key "II" :answ