\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot j&=0\\\\8 x - 4 y&=0\\\\y&=2x\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSubstituting $y=2x$ into the equation of our curve gives:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}1(2x)^{2}+4x(2x)-4x^{2}-8&=0\\\\8x^{2}-8&=0\\\\x^{2}&=1\\\\x&=\\pm 1\\end{aligned}$$\n\nFinally, the corresponding points are $(1,2)$ and $(-1,-2)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521800 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84245283-3cf9-5889-8c42-896a0c8af291" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points on a Curve at which the Tangent Vector is Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "306ad61b-7cf2-5e46-b92a-99bb59b27116" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521779} {:answer/id #uuid "a5d14569-99f9-5f0a-b34b-fcf4aef8d5b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "306ad61b-7cf2-5e46-b92a-99bb59b27116" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521779} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bf8aaf8-fe3e-5ed9-9824-d9ba6d421a9e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521776} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04f0e009-6fcf-56c0-ab31-f7119fd2b704" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521748} {:answer/id #uuid "bc7dfc78-e18a-5790-b5c3-ca2284d7c7cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521845}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04f0e009-6fcf-56c0-ab31-f7119fd2b704" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521748} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cc7bde4-9ea5-57bc-8ce3-0de4156021db" :answer-field/key "VI" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521778} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd4b8f