ype {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521824} {:answer/id #uuid "d3cf240d-8708-5599-aca2-d261591ea7e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521857}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92e10c0d-3823-528f-87a3-277e9336972f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521824} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9e874dd-4e18-58ae-af29-7f29c7c49fd9" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521864}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "638eb9ae-09f8-5fce-b7bc-2aac37c3181f" :question/problem "At which points on the curve $8 x y + 2 y^{2}=16 x^{2} + 48$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $j$?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $(-1,-4)$\n- **II.** $(0,4)$\n- **III.** $(\\frac{1}{2},4)$\n- **IV.** $(1,0)$\n- **V.** $(1,2)$\n- **VI.** $(1,4)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}8 x y + 2 y^{2}&=16 x^{2} + 48\\\\- 16 x^{2} + 8 x y + 2 y^{2} - 48&=0\\end{aligned}$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)=- 16 x^{2} + 8 x y + 2 y^{2} - 48$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$\n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$t(x,y)=f_y(x,y)\\,i-f_x(x,y)\\,j$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)&=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- 16 x^{2} + 8 x y + 2 y^{2} - 48)\\,i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- 16 x^{2} + 8 x y + 2 y^{2} - 48)\\,j\\\\&=(8 x + 4 y)\\,i-(- 32 x + 8 y)\\,j\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSince our tangent vector needs to be perpendicular to $j$, we must have $t\\cdot j=0.$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot j&=0\\\\32 x - 8 y&=0\\\\y&=4x\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSubstituting $y=4x$ into the equation of our curve gives:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}2(4x)^{2}+8x(4x)-16x^{2}-48&=0\\\\48x^{2}-48&=0\\\\x^{2}&=1\\\\x&=\\pm 1\\end{aligned}$$\n\nFinally, the corresponding points are $(1,4)$ and $(-1,-4)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521812 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84245283-3cf9-5889-8c42-896a0c8af291" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points on a Curve at which the Tangent Vector is Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a57fa11-825b-5d72-897b-0173f47e260f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(4,-4)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521766} {:answer/id #uuid "2165a269-3f7c-5aba-b78b-82d4e0f644ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-4,4)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521770} {:answer/id #uuid "55c4f24c-6643-5605-81fb-7978b6d363b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-4,0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521803} {:answer/id #uuid "6b1fa8ea-2503-52d0-b202-c7610a2fcdaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-4,-4)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521809} {:answer/id #uuid "d2ccf363-a0bd-5a86-90cc-34fb5f55c5a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-12,12)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521855}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2165a269-3f7c-5aba-b78b-82d4e0f644ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-4,4)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521770} :answer-field/id #uuid "2283f6dd-22a1-5e6f-b61e-5ea5da67f7c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521771}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "714feb07-8211-5226-a523-87577689d617" :question/problem "At which point on the curve $8 x y + 4 y^{2}=- 4 x^{2} + 3 y - 12$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $j$?" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}8 x y + 4 y^{2}&=- 4 x^{2} + 3 y - 12\\\\4 x^{2} + 8 x y + 4 y^{2} - 3 y + 12&=0\\end{aligned}$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)=4 x^{2} + 8 x y + 4 y^{2} - 3 y + 12$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$\n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$t(x,y)=f_y(x,y)\\,i-f_x(x,y)\\,j$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)&=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4 x^{2} + 8 x y + 4 y^{2} - 3 y + 12)\\,i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4 x^{2} + 8 x y + 4 y^{2} - 3 y + 12)\\,j\\\\&=(8 x + 8 y - 3)\\,i-(8 x + 8 y)\\,j\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSince our tangent vector needs to be perpendicular to $j$, we must have $t\\cdot j=0.$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot j&=0\\\\- 8 x - 8 y&=0\\\\y&=-x\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSubstituting $y=-x$ into the equation of our curve gives:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}4(x+(-x))^{2}-3(-x)-(-12)&=0\\\\3x-(-12)&=0\\\\3x&=-12\\\\x&=-4\\end{aligned}$$\n\nFinally, the corresponding point is $(-4,4)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521815 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84245283-3cf9-5889-8c42-896a0c8af291" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points on a Curve at which the Tangent Vector is Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fca5786-6f95-5edc-89d7-025c97273124" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(12,-12)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521757} {:answer/id #uuid "4d04ae77-6226-5ce7-885b-f80ba15e2fbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(6,-6)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521794} {:answer/id #uuid "5564689e-d3ce-5a9f-a719-7eb39d492591" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(6,6)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521801} {:answer/id #uuid "9771a166-dec6-517f-84ff-1a74c2c15214" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(6,0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521826} {:answer/id #uuid "c971a363-ecc3-50ee-89d0-484b756504a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-6,6)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521851}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d04ae77-6226-5ce7-885b-f80ba15e2fbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(6,-6)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521794} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef88e170-4022-53af-bd77-e7b6f6076c55" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521868}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "76dd91ba-d91e-5c6c-a612-22de10fca4c2" :question/problem "At which point on the curve $8 x y + 4 y^{2}=- 4 x^{2} + 2 y + 12$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $j$?" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}8 x y + 4 y^{2}&=- 4 x^{2} + 2 y + 12\\\\4 x^{2} + 8 x y + 4 y^{2} - 2 y - 12&=0\\end{aligned}$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)=4 x^{2} + 8 x y + 4 y^{2} - 2 y - 12$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$\n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$t(x,y)=f_y(x,y)\\,i-f_x(x,y)\\,j$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)&=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4 x^{2} + 8 x y + 4 y^{2} - 2 y - 12)\\,i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4 x^{2} + 8 x y + 4 y^{2} - 2 y - 12)\\,j\\\\&=(8 x + 8 y - 2)\\,i-(8 x + 8 y)\\,j\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSince our tangent vector needs to be perpendicular to $j$, we must have $t\\cdot j=0.$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot j&=0\\\\- 8 x - 8 y&=0\\\\y&=-x\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSubstituting $y=-x$ into the equation of our curve gives:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}4(x+(-x))^{2}-2(-x)-(12)&=0\\\\2x-(12)&=0\\\\2x&=12\\\\x&=6\\end{aligned}$$\n\nFinally, the corresponding point is $(6,-6)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521832 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84245283-3cf9-5889-8c42-896a0c8af291" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points on a Curve at which the Tangent Vector is Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36239cce-902e-52a9-b49c-e42a6bc1c132" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(3,-3)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521783} {:answer/id #uuid "67333ad8-5fc4-5f22-abf5-77c6242dbc74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-12,12)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521808} {:answer/id #uuid "9f7e2fdc-5342-51c3-9ca1-bc037dcd0169" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-3,-3)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521829} {:answer/id #uuid "aeabbe9c-35f7-56c8-9956-5f4b302d43d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-3,3)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521842} {:answer/id #uuid "fb340755-5a6e-525b-9533-8be7ec844986" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-3,0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521874}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aeabbe9c-35f7-56c8-9956-5f4b302d43d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-3,3)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521842} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac6736fd-7e64-5c2d-8cf8-ffbe9d4a8da2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521838}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a3e58fdb-d0b9-56b1-bc61-4cc0137e18be" :question/problem "At which point on the curve $8 x y + 4 y^{2}=- 4 x^{2} + 4 y - 12$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $j$?" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}8 x y + 4 y^{2}&=- 4 x^{2} + 4 y - 12\\\\4 x^{2} + 8 x y + 4 y^{2} - 4 y + 12&=0\\end{aligned}$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)=4 x^{2} + 8 x y + 4 y^{2} - 4 y + 12$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$\n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$t(x,y)=f_y(x,y)\\,i-f_x(x,y)\\,j$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)&=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4 x^{2} + 8 x y + 4 y^{2} - 4 y + 12)\\,i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4 x^{2} + 8 x y + 4 y^{2} - 4 y + 12)\\,j\\\\&=(8 x + 8 y - 4)\\,i-(8 x + 8 y)\\,j\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSince our tangent vector needs to be perpendicular to $j$, we must have $t\\cdot j=0.$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot j&=0\\\\- 8 x - 8 y&=0\\\\y&=-x\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSubstituting $y=-x$ into the equation of our curve gives:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}4(x+(-x))^{2}-4(-x)-(-12)&=0\\\\4x-(-12)&=0\\\\4x&=-12\\\\x&=-3\\end{aligned}$$\n\nFinally, the corresponding point is $(-3,3)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521863 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84245283-3cf9-5889-8c42-896a0c8af291" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points on a Curve at which the Tangent Vector is Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c751557-77e8-5772-8224-bcd8b52ba3c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-5,5)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521777} {:answer/id #uuid "3c9640d8-fe2b-5a2c-9bf2-1921afc58809" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-5,-5)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521786} {:answer/id #uuid "912504b1-f9c3-5d19-8f90-fc428ccbb006" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(5,-5)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521822} {:answer/id #uuid "ae59b4c0-93bd-5c71-bcd3-142c6d6eb995" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-15,15)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521841} {:answer/id #uuid "ccac1d60-6b01-5598-82a2-30b9d00efbf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-5,0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521853}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c751557-77e8-5772-8224-bcd8b52ba3c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-5,5)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521777} :answer-field/id #uuid "a368d38c-2b11-5487-a14f-a13efc2b6541" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521831}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e7a17a4a-d80f-51f1-afa6-1faeaa5943f8" :question/problem "At which point on the curve $2 x y + y^{2}=- x^{2} + 3 y - 15$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $j$?" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}2 x y + y^{2}&=- x^{2} + 3 y - 15\\\\x^{2} + 2 x y + y^{2} - 3 y + 15&=0\\end{aligned}$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)=x^{2} + 2 x y + y^{2} - 3 y + 15$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$\n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$t(x,y)=f_y(x,y)\\,i-f_x(x,y)\\,j$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)&=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x^{2} + 2 x y + y^{2} - 3 y + 15)\\,i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2} + 2 x y + y^{2} - 3 y + 15)\\,j\\\\&=(2 x + 2 y - 3)\\,i-(2 x + 2 y)\\,j\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSince our tangent vector needs to be perpendicular to $j$, we must have $t\\cdot j=0.$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot j&=0\\\\- 2 x - 2 y&=0\\\\y&=-x\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSubstituting $y=-x$ into the equation of our curve gives:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}1(x+(-x))^{2}-3(-x)-(-15)&=0\\\\3x-(-15)&=0\\\\3x&=-15\\\\x&=-5\\end{aligned}$$\n\nFinally, the corresponding point is $(-5,5)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521870 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84245283-3cf9-5889-8c42-896a0c8af291" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points on a Curve at which the Tangent Vector is Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f4e1d8e-84d6-5a20-9c01-8ae98987f8dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521811} {:answer/id #uuid "c087c404-166b-5d66-9df7-23a64d6373c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c087c404-166b-5d66-9df7-23a64d6373c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :a